tcome and one zero. The sum of pairwise differences is the same regardless of which lottery is chosen — it's symmetric. Therefore, the sum of pairwise differences is identical for both lotteries. Thus, the decision reason would be indifferent between A and B. However, the reason is defined to prefer the one with the more favorable sum. Since both have the same sum, the reason does not favor either. Therefore, the decision reason is applicable to the problem and can be evaluated based on whether the individual considered this sum of differences.",
